values
  ('p-momotaro-salve', 'Momotaro Apotheca Soothe & Restore Salve', 'Momotaro Apotheca', 'intimate-care', 'physical', 'A certified organic balm for the vulva that Momotaro Apotheca says comforts dryness, itching and irritation, including irritation that comes with yeast infections and bacterial vaginosis. Coconut and jojoba oils form the base, with goldenseal, Oregon grape, echinacea, calendula and tea tree. The brand says it is safe for daily use and during flare-ups. Free of alcohol, parabens, phthalates, silicone, sulfates and synthetic fragrance.', '$37 (30 mL)', '/products/momotaro/salve.webp', 'https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/salve', '["discomfort","comfort","organic","hormone-free","external-only"]'::jsonb, '["vaginal-health"]'::jsonb, '["momotaroapotheca.com"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Sold as a topical balm. momotaroapotheca.com does not describe it as FDA-cleared or approved, and it does not appear in FDA''s drug listings under Momotaro Apotheca (checked on openFDA 2026-10-17).","materials":"30 mL (1 oz) jar. Ingredients: organic coconut oil, organic kokum butter, organic beeswax, organic jojoba, organic tea tree, organic goldenseal, organic echinacea, organic calendula, organic Oregon grape.","recalls":"No recalls found.","sideEffects":"Tea tree oil can cause redness or irritation in some people, per NIH. Contains goldenseal, which NIH says people who are pregnant or breastfeeding should not use. Full warnings are listed below.","opinionAlerts":"The brand markets the salve for yeast infections, BV and UTIs. Those are its own claims; momotaroapotheca.com cites no published study of this product."}'::jsonb, 'A plant-oil balm can be a gentle way to protect dry or chafed vulvar skin. The brand also says its goldenseal and Oregon grape target yeast and bacteria, but momotaroapotheca.com cites no published study of this product, so treat that as the brand''s claim.

Two ingredient notes from NIH: tea tree oil applied to skin is usually fine but can cause redness or irritation in some people, and people who are pregnant or breastfeeding should not use goldenseal.

Itching, burning or unusual discharge can come from a yeast infection, BV or a sexually transmitted infection, and these need different treatments. If symptoms are new, keep coming back, or don''t clear up, see a clinician for a diagnosis.', 'Rated 4.92 out of 5 from 504 reviews on momotaroapotheca.com''s own review widget (brand-hosted, not independent).', 'momotaroapotheca.com cites no published study of this product. Its claims about yeast infections, BV and UTIs are the brand''s own.', 'independent', 'ayna summary of NIH (NCCIH) safety information on the ingredients. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"doctorOpinionShort":"A plant-oil balm for dry, irritated vulvar skin. The brand''s infection claims aren''t backed by a published study of the product, it contains tea tree oil (can irritate) and goldenseal (NIH says avoid in pregnancy and breastfeeding).","doctorOpinionCitations":[{"url":"https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/tea-tree-oil","label":"NIH (NCCIH): Tea Tree Oil"},{"url":"https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/goldenseal","label":"NIH (NCCIH): Goldenseal"}],"whoItsFor":["Vulvar dryness, itching or irritation","Chafing and sensitivity from sex, tight clothing, sweat or exercise","People who want a fragrance-free, organic balm for external intimate skin","Not the pick if you are pregnant or breastfeeding: it contains goldenseal, which NIH says to avoid then"],"howToUse":{"intro":"Per Momotaro Apotheca''s own directions:","steps":["With clean hands, apply a pea-sized amount around the vulva or affected area.","Use as needed, for everyday support or during flare-ups.","The brand recommends use over 60 to 90 days for best results."],"sourceUrl":"https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/salve","sourceLabel":"momotaroapotheca.com: Soothe & Restore Salve"},"warnings":["For external use only. Avoid contact with eyes.","Stop using it if irritation occurs.","Pregnant, breastfeeding, or under medical care: talk to your provider first. NIH says not to use goldenseal while pregnant or breastfeeding.","If symptoms persist or worsen, see a healthcare professional.","Keep out of reach of children."],"ingredients":"Organic coconut oil, kokum butter, beeswax, jojoba, tea tree, goldenseal, echinacea, calendula, Oregon grape.","scientificCitations":[],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[]},"community":{"links":[{"platform":"website","url":"https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/salve","text":"momotaroapotheca.com: Soothe & Restore Salve","summary":"The brand''s product page, with ingredients, directions, warnings and its on-site reviews."}]}},"isEmergingBrand":true}'::jsonb),
  ('p-momotaro-daily-probiotic', 'Momotaro Apotheca Daily Probiotic', 'Momotaro Apotheca', 'supplement', 'physical', 'A once-a-day probiotic with 25 billion cultures from 10 strains of Lactobacillus and Bifidobacterium, including L. crispatus, L. gasseri and L. rhamnosus. Momotaro Apotheca says it supports the gut, the immune system and the vaginal microbiome. Vegan, shelf-stable, and free of gluten, soy and preservatives. 30 capsules, a one-month supply.', '$49 (30 capsules)', '/products/momotaro/daily-probiotic.webp', 'https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/probiotic', '["supplement","vegan"]'::jsonb, '["vaginal-health","supplement"]'::jsonb, '["momotaroapotheca.com"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Sold as a dietary supplement. The label says its statements have not been evaluated by the FDA and that it is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.","materials":"30 capsules. Strains: Lactobacillus acidophilus, L. plantarum, L. reuteri, L. crispatus, Bifidobacterium lactis, L. gasseri, L. paracasei, L. rhamnosus, L. brevis, B. longum. Other ingredients: microcrystalline cellulose, vegetable cellulose (capsule), silica.","recalls":"No recalls found.","sideEffects":"Intended for adults. Talk to your provider before use if pregnant, breastfeeding, or taking medication, per the brand. Full warnings are listed below.","opinionAlerts":"The brand says the formula helps protect against pH imbalance, BV, UTIs and yeast infections. Those are its own claims; momotaroapotheca.com cites no published study of this product."}'::jsonb, 'This probiotic includes several Lactobacillus strains that are found in a healthy vagina, which is the idea behind the brand''s vaginal-health claims. NIH notes that different probiotic strains can have different effects, so a benefit found for one strain doesn''t carry over to another, and momotaroapotheca.com cites no published study of this particular blend.

A probiotic is not a treatment for an active infection. If you have symptoms of BV, a yeast infection or a UTI, see a clinician for a diagnosis.', 'Rated 4.96 out of 5 from 46 reviews on momotaroapotheca.com''s own review widget (brand-hosted, not independent).', 'momotaroapotheca.com cites no published study of this blend. NIH notes probiotic effects depend on the specific strain.', 'independent', 'ayna summary of NIH (NCCIH) information on probiotics. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"doctorOpinionShort":"Contains vaginal Lactobacillus strains, but NIH notes probiotic effects are strain-specific and no study of this blend is cited. Not a treatment for an active infection.","doctorOpinionCitations":[{"url":"https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/probiotics-what-you-need-to-know","label":"NIH (NCCIH): Probiotics, what you need to know"}],"whoItsFor":["Adults who want a daily probiotic aimed at both gut and vaginal health","People who prefer a vegan, shelf-stable capsule","Not a treatment for an active infection: see a clinician if you have symptoms"],"howToUse":{"intro":"Per Momotaro Apotheca''s own directions:","steps":["Take one capsule a day with a meal, or within 30 minutes of eating.","Take it at about the same time each day.","The brand says to use it for at least 90 days to notice most benefits."],"sourceUrl":"https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/probiotic","sourceLabel":"momotaroapotheca.com: Daily Probiotic"},"warnings":["Intended for adults. Keep out of reach of children.","Pregnant, breastfeeding, or taking medication: talk to your provider before use.","A probiotic doesn''t treat an active infection. See a clinician for symptoms of BV, a yeast infection or a UTI."],"ingredients":"25 billion cultures: L. acidophilus, L. plantarum, L. reuteri, L. crispatus, B. lactis, L. gasseri, L. paracasei, L. rhamnosus, L. brevis, B. longum.","scientificCitations":[],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[]},"community":{"links":[{"platform":"website","url":"https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/probiotic","text":"momotaroapotheca.com: Daily Probiotic","summary":"The brand''s product page, with the strain list, directions, label statements and its on-site reviews."}]}},"isEmergingBrand":true}'::jsonb),
  ('p-momotaro-urinary-tract-supplement', 'Momotaro Apotheca Urinary Tract & Pelvic Health Super Supplement', 'Momotaro Apotheca', 'supplement', 'physical', 'A plant-based capsule with D-mannose, cranberry fruit concentrate (3,000 mg, per the brand), Oregon grape root, uva ursi (bearberry) and marshmallow root. Momotaro Apotheca designed it for times of urinary discomfort and says it supports UTIs, bladder discomfort, interstitial cystitis, BV and yeast imbalance. 60 vegan capsules.', '$35 (60 capsules)', '/products/momotaro/urinary-tract-supplement.webp', 'https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/the-uti-supplement', '["uti","supplement","vegan"]'::jsonb, '["uti-prevention","supplement"]'::jsonb, '["momotaroapotheca.com"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Sold as a dietary supplement. The brand says its statements have not been evaluated by the FDA and that it is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.","materials":"60 vegetarian capsules. Ingredients: D-mannose, cranberry fruit (Vaccinium macrocarpon), Oregon grape (Mahonia aquifolium), bearberry (Arctostaphylos uva-ursi), marshmallow root (Althaea officinalis), brown rice flour, rice hulls, vegetarian capsule.","recalls":"No recalls found.","sideEffects":"The brand says it is meant for times of urinary discomfort, not continuous long-term use, because of the uva ursi. Cranberry may interact with the blood thinner warfarin, per NIH. Full warnings are listed below.","opinionAlerts":"The brand says it \"supports UTIs\". NIH says cranberry may help prevent repeat UTIs in some women but is not recommended as a treatment for an existing UTI."}'::jsonb, 'Cranberry has the most research of the ingredients here. NIH says cranberry products may lower the risk of repeat UTIs in women by about 25 percent, but findings are inconsistent, and cranberry is not recommended as a treatment for an existing UTI. NIH also says anyone who thinks they have a UTI should see a provider, and not use cranberry instead of a proven treatment.

The brand notes that uva ursi is meant for short-term use during urinary discomfort, not long-term use. Oregon grape is a source of berberine, per the brand, and NIH warns that berberine (in goldenseal) can be harmful to newborns, so check with a provider before using this while pregnant or breastfeeding.

An untreated UTI can spread to the kidneys. Fever, back or side pain, or blood in your urine need medical care right away.', 'Rated 4.94 out of 5 from 68 reviews on momotaroapotheca.com''s own review widget (brand-hosted, not independent).', 'momotaroapotheca.com cites no published study of this blend. For cranberry, NIH says it may lower the risk of repeat UTIs in some women, with inconsistent findings, and doesn''t treat an existing UTI.', 'independent', 'ayna summary of NIH (NCCIH) information on cranberry and goldenseal. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"doctorOpinionShort":"NIH says cranberry may help prevent repeat UTIs in some women but doesn''t treat an existing one. Short-term use only (uva ursi), and check with a provider if pregnant or breastfeeding.","doctorOpinionCitations":[{"url":"https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/cranberry","label":"NIH (NCCIH): Cranberry"},{"url":"https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/goldenseal","label":"NIH (NCCIH): Goldenseal (berberine and newborns)"}],"whoItsFor":["Adults who want a plant-based supplement during times of urinary discomfort","People with repeat UTIs who want to try cranberry and D-mannose alongside their clinician''s plan","Not a replacement for antibiotics if you have a UTI: see a provider for diagnosis and treatment","Not for long-term daily use, per the brand, because it contains uva ursi"],"howToUse":{"intro":"Per Momotaro Apotheca''s own directions:","steps":["For acute discomfort, take \"up to 8x with a large glass of water 2-3 times a day,\" as the brand puts it, or as directed by your healthcare practitioner.","Use it during times of urinary discomfort, not continuously over a long period.","If symptoms keep coming back, the brand recommends talking to a healthcare provider."],"sourceUrl":"https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/the-uti-supplement","sourceLabel":"momotaroapotheca.com: Urinary Tract & Pelvic Health Super Supplement"},"warnings":["Not a treatment for an existing UTI. Fever, back or side pain, or blood in your urine need medical care right away.","Designed for short-term use, not continuous long-term use (it contains uva ursi), per the brand.","Taking warfarin or other medicines: ask your provider first; NIH notes cranberry may interact with warfarin.","Pregnant or breastfeeding: ask your provider first.","Intended for adults. Keep out of reach of children."],"ingredients":"D-mannose, cranberry fruit concentrate, Oregon grape root, uva ursi (bearberry leaf), marshmallow root.","scientificCitations":[],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[]},"community":{"links":[{"platform":"website","url":"https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/the-uti-supplement","text":"momotaroapotheca.com: Urinary Tract & Pelvic Health Super Supplement","summary":"The brand''s product page, with ingredients, directions, its uva ursi note and its on-site reviews."}]}},"isEmergingBrand":true}'::jsonb),
  ('p-momotaro-vaginal-suppository', 'Momotaro Apotheca Vaginal Suppository', 'Momotaro Apotheca', 'intimate-care', 'physical', 'A homeopathic vaginal suppository that Momotaro Apotheca markets for yeast infections, BV and vaginal irritation, calling it a natural alternative to antibiotics and antifungals. The base is cocoa butter, coconut oil, beeswax and jojoba with Oregon grape, calendula, echinacea and tea tree. 14 suppositories (2 mL each). The brand suggests storing it somewhere cool, like the fridge.', '$48 (14 suppositories)', '/products/momotaro/vaginal-suppository.webp', 'https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/the-suppository', '["discomfort","organic","hormone-free"]'::jsonb, '["vaginal-health"]'::jsonb, '["momotaroapotheca.com"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Listed with the FDA as an unapproved homeopathic over-the-counter drug (NDC 83385-001; active ingredients Echinacea purpurea, wood creosote and Thuja occidentalis, each at 12X). FDA says homeopathic products sold in the US have not been reviewed by the FDA for safety or effectiveness.","materials":"14 suppositories, 2 mL each. Ingredients: organic beechwood (Kreosotum), organic beeswax, organic calendula, organic cocoa butter, organic coconut oil, organic echinacea, organic jojoba oil, organic northern white cedar (Thuja occidentalis), organic Oregon grape, organic tea tree oil.","recalls":"No recalls found.","sideEffects":"Contains tea tree oil, which can cause redness or irritation in some people, per NIH. The product page lists no warnings; read the carton. Full warnings are listed below.","opinionAlerts":"FDA warns that people may use unapproved homeopathic drugs instead of proven treatments, which can delay effective treatment. The brand''s infection claims are its own."}'::jsonb, 'This is a homeopathic drug. FDA lists it as unapproved, and FDA says homeopathic products have not been reviewed for safety or effectiveness. FDA also warns that using an unapproved homeopathic product instead of a proven treatment can delay care that works.

Yeast infections and BV have similar symptoms but need different treatments, and proven over-the-counter and prescription options exist for both. If this is your first infection, symptoms keep coming back, or they don''t clear up within a week, see a clinician for a diagnosis.

The suppository contains tea tree oil, which NIH says can cause redness or irritation in some people.', 'Rated 4.81 out of 5 from 32 reviews on momotaroapotheca.com''s own review widget (brand-hosted, not independent).', 'momotaroapotheca.com cites no published study of this product, and FDA has not reviewed it for safety or effectiveness.', 'independent', 'ayna summary of FDA guidance on homeopathic products and NIH (NCCIH) information on tea tree oil. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', true, false, null, true, '{"doctorOpinionShort":"An FDA-listed but unapproved homeopathic drug; FDA hasn''t reviewed homeopathic products for safety or effectiveness. Don''t let it delay a diagnosis or a proven treatment.","doctorOpinionCitations":[{"url":"https://www.fda.gov/drugs/information-drug-class/homeopathic-products","label":"FDA: Homeopathic Products"},{"url":"https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/tea-tree-oil","label":"NIH (NCCIH): Tea Tree Oil"}],"whoItsFor":["People who want a plant-based, hormone-free option for vaginal irritation and have talked it through with a clinician","Not the pick for a first-time or recurring infection without a diagnosis: yeast infections and BV need different, proven treatments"],"howToUse":{"intro":"Per Momotaro Apotheca''s own directions:","steps":["For acute issues, insert one vaginally twice a day for 5 to 7 days until symptoms clear.","It can also be used as needed for discomfort.","The brand suggests pairing it with its Salve.","Store somewhere cool and dry, like the refrigerator; the natural ingredients can separate."],"sourceUrl":"https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/the-suppository","sourceLabel":"momotaroapotheca.com: Vaginal Suppository"},"warnings":["A homeopathic product the FDA has not reviewed for safety or effectiveness. Don''t use it instead of a proven treatment.","First infection, symptoms that come back, or symptoms that don''t clear in a week: see a clinician.","Fever, pelvic pain, or unusual discharge with a bad smell: see a clinician.","Pregnant or breastfeeding: talk to your provider before using any vaginal product.","Stop using it if irritation occurs."],"ingredients":"Homeopathic actives (12X): Echinacea purpurea, wood creosote (beechwood), Thuja occidentalis. Base: cocoa butter, coconut oil, beeswax, jojoba, Oregon grape, calendula, tea tree.","scientificCitations":[],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[]},"community":{"links":[{"platform":"website","url":"https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/the-suppository","text":"momotaroapotheca.com: Vaginal Suppository","summary":"The brand''s product page, with ingredients, directions and its on-site reviews."}]}},"isEmergingBrand":true}'::jsonb),
  ('p-momotaro-hydrosol-toner', 'Momotaro Apotheca Organic Hydrosol Toner', 'Momotaro Apotheca', 'intimate-care', 'physical', 'An alcohol-free micromist of steam-distilled organic orange blossom, rose, rosemary and lavender waters. Momotaro Apotheca says it soothes irritation, neutralizes odor and hydrates the face, body and external pelvic area, for use after a shower, workout, period or sex. Certified organic, vegan and cruelty-free.', '$56', '/products/momotaro/hydrosol-toner.webp', 'https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/hydrosol', '["comfort","organic","vegan","external-only"]'::jsonb, '["vaginal-health","skin-hair"]'::jsonb, '["momotaroapotheca.com"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Sold as a cosmetic body mist. momotaroapotheca.com does not describe it as FDA-cleared or approved, and it does not appear in FDA''s drug listings under Momotaro Apotheca (checked on openFDA 2026-10-17).","materials":"Ingredients: organic orange blossom (Citrus aurantium amara), organic rose water (Rosa damascena), organic rosemary distillate, organic lavender distillate, glyceryl caprylate, glyceryl undecylenate (both derived from coconut and castor).","recalls":"No recalls found.","sideEffects":"Stop using it if irritation occurs. Full warnings are listed below.","opinionAlerts":"Claims about calming inflammation and odor-causing bacteria are the brand''s own; momotaroapotheca.com cites no published study of this product."}'::jsonb, 'A water-based floral mist for external skin, including the outer pelvic area, with no alcohol or synthetic fragrance, per the brand. Momotaro Apotheca says the botanical waters help calm irritation and odor, but cites no published study of this product.

A change in vaginal odor, especially a fishy smell or with unusual discharge, can be a sign of BV or another infection. A mist won''t treat that; see a clinician.', 'Rated 4.85 out of 5 from 34 reviews on momotaroapotheca.com''s own review widget (brand-hosted, not independent).', 'momotaroapotheca.com cites no published study of this product.', 'brand', 'Sourced only from Momotaro Apotheca''s own site, not independent clinical literature.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"doctorOpinionShort":"An alcohol-free floral mist for external skin. Its odor and irritation claims are the brand''s own; a new odor with discharge needs a clinician, not a spray.","doctorOpinionCitations":[{"url":"https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/hydrosol","label":"momotaroapotheca.com: where the brand presents these claims"}],"whoItsFor":["People who want a refreshing, alcohol-free mist after showering, exercise, a period or sex","Skin folds and areas prone to sweat, chafing or ingrown hairs, per the brand","For external use: not for inside the vagina"],"howToUse":{"intro":"Per Momotaro Apotheca''s own directions:","steps":["Hold a few inches from clean skin and mist the face, body or external pelvic area.","Spray into skin folds and areas prone to sweat or irritation.","Let it air dry. Use daily or as needed."],"sourceUrl":"https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/hydrosol","sourceLabel":"momotaroapotheca.com: Organic Hydrosol Toner"},"warnings":["For external use only.","Stop using it if irritation occurs.","A new vaginal odor with unusual discharge can mean an infection: see a clinician."],"ingredients":"Organic orange blossom, rose, rosemary and lavender distillates; glyceryl caprylate and glyceryl undecylenate.","scientificCitations":[],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[]},"community":{"links":[{"platform":"website","url":"https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/hydrosol","text":"momotaroapotheca.com: Organic Hydrosol Toner","summary":"The brand''s product page, with ingredients, directions and its on-site reviews."}]}},"isEmergingBrand":true}'::jsonb),
  ('p-momotaro-bath-body-tonic', 'Momotaro Apotheca Nourishing Bath & Body Tonic', 'Momotaro Apotheca', 'intimate-care', 'physical', 'A jojoba-oil concentrate with tea tree, cedarwood and sweet orange essential oils and infusions of goldenseal and Oregon grape. Momotaro Apotheca says to add it to a warm bath, or use it as a spot treatment for irritation, ingrown hairs and razor burn. Not for internal use. 55 mL (1.9 fl oz).', '$48 (55 mL)', '/products/momotaro/bath-body-tonic.webp', 'https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/tonic', '["comfort","organic","vegan","external-only"]'::jsonb, '["vaginal-health","skin-hair"]'::jsonb, '["momotaroapotheca.com"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Sold as a bath and body oil. momotaroapotheca.com does not describe it as FDA-cleared or approved, and it does not appear in FDA''s drug listings under Momotaro Apotheca (checked on openFDA 2026-10-17).","materials":"55 mL (1.9 fl oz). Ingredients: organic jojoba oil, organic tea tree essential oil, cedarwood Virginia (Juniperus virginiana) essential oil, organic sweet orange essential oil, infusion of goldenseal leaf, Oregon grape.","recalls":"No recalls found.","sideEffects":"Tea tree oil can cause redness or irritation in some people, and should never be swallowed, per NIH. Contains goldenseal, which NIH says people who are pregnant or breastfeeding should not use. Full warnings are listed below.","opinionAlerts":"The brand markets it as a spot treatment for discomfort from yeast and bacterial infections. Those are its own claims; momotaroapotheca.com cites no published study of this product."}'::jsonb, 'A jojoba-based oil for the bath or for spot use on skin, including after shaving. The brand says its goldenseal and Oregon grape help with yeast and bacterial infections, but cites no published study of this product.

NIH notes that tea tree oil can irritate skin and should never be swallowed, and that people who are pregnant or breastfeeding should not use goldenseal. The brand itself says it is not for internal use and to avoid broken skin and mucous membranes.', 'Rated 4.9 out of 5 from 58 reviews on momotaroapotheca.com''s own review widget (brand-hosted, not independent).', 'momotaroapotheca.com cites no published study of this product. Its infection claims are the brand''s own.', 'independent', 'ayna summary of NIH (NCCIH) safety information on the ingredients. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"doctorOpinionShort":"A bath and spot oil with tea tree (can irritate) and goldenseal (NIH says avoid in pregnancy and breastfeeding). Not for internal use; infection claims are the brand''s own.","doctorOpinionCitations":[{"url":"https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/tea-tree-oil","label":"NIH (NCCIH): Tea Tree Oil"},{"url":"https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/goldenseal","label":"NIH (NCCIH): Goldenseal"}],"whoItsFor":["People who want a fragrance-free, organic bath oil","Spot care for ingrown hairs and razor burn, per the brand","Not the pick if you are pregnant or breastfeeding: it contains goldenseal, which NIH says to avoid then"],"howToUse":{"intro":"Per Momotaro Apotheca''s own directions:","steps":["Add 5 to 10 droppers-full to a clean, warm bath and soak.","Or apply as a spot treatment for blemishes or ingrown hairs, or as a pre-, during- or post-shave oil.","Shake gently before use; the oils can separate naturally.","Not for internal use. Avoid broken skin and mucous membranes."],"sourceUrl":"https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/tonic","sourceLabel":"momotaroapotheca.com: Nourishing Bath & Body Tonic"},"warnings":["For external use only. Not for internal use; avoid broken skin and mucous membranes.","Avoid contact with eyes. Stop using it if irritation occurs.","Never swallow: it contains tea tree oil.","Pregnant, breastfeeding, or under medical care: talk to your provider first. NIH says not to use goldenseal while pregnant or breastfeeding.","Keep out of reach of children."],"ingredients":"Organic jojoba oil, tea tree, cedarwood and sweet orange essential oils, goldenseal leaf infusion, Oregon grape.","scientificCitations":[],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[]},"community":{"links":[{"platform":"website","url":"https://momotaroapotheca.com/products/tonic","text":"momotaroapotheca.com: Nourishing Bath & Body Tonic","summary":"The brand''s product page, with ingredients, directions, warnings and its on-site reviews."}]}},"isEmergingBrand":true}'::jsonb)
